  "notes": "A technical term used primarily in science, medicine, and engineering to describe substances passing through materials. The verb form {透過|とうか}する takes the thing being transmitted as the subject and the medium with the particle を.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {光|ひかり}を{透過|とうか}する: to transmit light\n- {透過|とうか}{率|りつ}: transmittance, transmission rate\n- {透過|とうか}{性|せい}: permeability\n- {透過|とうか}{型|がた}: transmission type (e.g., {透過|とうか}{型|がた}{電子|でんし}{顕微鏡|けんびきょう}, transmission electron microscope)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {浸透|しんとう}: permeation, infiltration — often implies gradual seeping into something; also used figuratively for ideas spreading\n- {通過|つうか}: passing through — used for physical passage of people or vehicles, not substances through materials\n- {投下|とうか}: dropping, release — a homophone with a completely different meaning",
